opEqFoldT -- SEQ 367 (Tony, 2026-10-16): the op= fold oddities, PINNED AT TODAY'S VALUES on the interpreted road
(jitOpEqFoldT is the jit road, its own process). Not cured -- fixit incant/fixits/opEqFoldsMidRun.
A compound assignment is folded MID-RUN as an arithmetic fold step instead of being split at the assignment tier, so:
  OF-1  a < b += 1      -> a 10 b 5. The tier tree is acK(a, <, acX(b, +=, 1)): the fold's running value starts as
        the FIELD b, so b is written. Intended: refused by name ("the left of += is a value, not a field"), b 4.
  OF-2  s + t += "x"    -> s ab t cd. Lands on runAccFold's acRun copy, as VT-8 does. Intended: refused, s ab t cd.
  OF-3  r = a < b += 1  -> r has no value and prints its own tag (ofQ). Intended: refused.
  OF-4  r = a + b += 1  -> a 10 r 15. Intended: refused, a 10.
a + b += 1 alone is valueTargetT VT-8 (interpreted, lands on the copy) and jitValueTargetT JVT-8 (jitted, refused) --
not duplicated here.
